## Building Queue[T] — FIFO

### The Generic Type

```xiom
type Queue[T] {
  items: Vec[T];
}
```

### Queue Operations

```xiom
fn Queue.enqueue[T](&mut self, item: T) {
  self.items.push(item);
}

fn Queue.dequeue[T](&mut self) -> Option[T] {
  if self.items.len() == 0 {
    return Option.None;
  };
  let result = self.items.get(0).unwrap().clone();
  self.items.remove(0);
  Option.Some(result)
}

fn Queue.front[T](&self) -> Option[&T] {
  if self.items.len() == 0 {
    return Option.None;
  };
  Option.Some(self.items.get(0).unwrap())
}

fn Queue.is_empty[T](&self) -> Bool {
  self.items.len() == 0
}
```

### Queue vs Stack

| Operation | Stack (LIFO) | Queue (FIFO) |
|-----------|-------------|-------------|
| Add | push (back) | enqueue (back) |
| Remove | pop (back) | dequeue (front) |
| Order | Last in, first out | First in, first out |

### Usage

```xiom
let mut q: Queue[Str] = Queue{ items: Vec[Str].new() };
q.enqueue("Alice");
q.enqueue("Bob");
q.enqueue("Carol");
// Alice is served first, then Bob, then Carol
```

